  "notes": [
    "ref rows come from a rerun after fixing the harness's element picker (merged row labels); locator and baseline rows are from the same full run.",
    "ref misses in the full run: minus:Laptop Stand (the agent closed the socket mid-request; no crash in the crash buffer; logcat had been cleared by the next launch, so the cause is unknown) and buy:Basic (no 'Buy' element in that snapshot, likely taken before the grid laid out). Both passed 3/3 when rerun alone.",
    "locator refusals are safe (typed not-found/ambiguous, no tap), but two are droidctl locator bugs: --desc does not match a desc merged from a child (Compose Icon inside a button: 'Settings', 'Star'), and --right-of/--left-of anchors must equal a whole merged row label ('Ada Lovelace \u00b7 Lunch tomorrow?'), not a part of it. buy:Basic/Standard with --below are genuinely ambiguous (two Buy buttons below in the same column).",
    "baseline = mobile-mcp 1.0.5 Android robot re-implemented (uiautomator dump + collectElements + input tap at rect centre); element chosen with the same rule as ref. mobile-mcp itself was not run (its device path requires the mobilecli binary, which can install an agent on the phone).",
